# History I/O failures: appends that fail during a turn, and history
# files serve cannot read, as the page and serve see them. One session,
# its child, the disk under ~/.bough/history, and the page open on the
# session. Every other spec assumes appends and history.Read succeed.
#
# This spec states what the product OWES. Where the code does something
# else today, the comment on the action says so ("Today: ..."); each of
# those is a one-line mutation of this spec that fizz rejects (see the
# invariants), so the Go MBT run of this spec is expected to go red there
# until the product is fixed.
#
# What the code does (read 2026-09-24, main 5471918e):
#
# - Store.Append (plugins/history/history.go) keeps the entry in memory
#   whatever happens, writes one JSON line through a bufio.Writer, and on
#   a write error Resets the writer (the lost line is dropped for good)
#   and reports the FIRST error of a run of failures to the error sink.
#   A later successful append clears `failing`. Nothing ever re-writes a
#   dropped line.
# - The ui row's sink (plugins/ui/live.go) publishes the error as a live
#   Event{Kind:"error", Text:"history not saved: ..."}; serve's pump turns
#   it into an "error" event on the session's stream. The page treats
#   every event except deltas/activity/call starts as a CHANGE SIGNAL and
#   refetches (app.tsx catchUp): the refetch reads the file, which does
#   not hold the error, so the page never says recording stopped.
# - A write that fails part way (ENOSPC after some bytes, or a crash
#   mid-write) leaves a fragment with no newline. s.off is not advanced
#   and the file is not truncated, so the next line is appended to the
#   fragment: one glued line, which readEntries skips as corrupt. The
#   entry written AFTER the failure is the one lost on read. Only
#   OpenExisting (resume) drops a torn tail (dropTornTail).
# - Status is derived from disk (internal/serve/status.go StatusOf): an
#   input with no done after it is running while the child lives and
#   interrupted once it is gone. A done that never reached disk therefore
#   reads running while the child idles and interrupted after it exits,
#   and the finished-turn signals (unseen, trouble) never fire.
# - history.List globs *.jsonl. filepath.Glob ignores I/O errors, so an
#   unreadable sessions dir lists as an EMPTY 200. A file readEntries
#   cannot read (chmod 000, or one line over the scanner's 4 MiB cap:
#   bufio.ErrTooLong) is skipped with a stderr note, so the session is
#   missing from the list, and api.info (which only looks in List, and
#   maps a List error to "not found" too) answers 404 "unknown session"
#   on GET /api/sessions/{id}, /events and every per-session verb.
#   OpenExisting fails on the same ErrTooLong, so the session cannot be
#   resumed while its file is intact. Nothing in history caps what
#   Append writes: a >4 MiB tool result writes a line history cannot
#   read back.
# - A corrupt line in the middle is skipped and the rest is read
#   (readEntries continues): that part holds today.
#
# What the spec asks for instead (the fixes the MBT stage will drive):
#
# - A failed append is kept PENDING in memory and re-written, in order,
#   before the next line and on a retry tick while the child lives
#   (Flush), after truncating any torn fragment back to the last
#   newline. So the disk catches up with the child once space frees, and
#   a finished turn does not stay running.
# - While entries are pending the page says history is not being saved
#   (warn). serve keeps it for the session after the child exits with
#   entries still pending (the loss is then permanent: DoneLost), until
#   a later child's append lands.
# - The list answers 500 with a reason when the dir cannot be read; a
#   session whose file exists is listed and opens, or answers 500 with a
#   reason (unreadable file); an entry of any size history wrote reads
#   back; a corrupt line hides nothing after it.
#
# Mapped model -> this spec:
# - Recording / WriteFails / TornOnDisk / GluedLine / DoneLost / TornTailLive
#   / CorruptMidLine / OversizeLine / FileUnreadable / DirUnreadable /
#   Repaired are values of disk, pending, tail, glued, child and fault.
# - ErrorEventOnly, GluedLine, SessionVanished_404, EmptyList200 are the
#   states the invariants forbid (reachable only in the mutations).
# - ErrorEvent is folded into the failing append: the event reaches the
#   subscribed page in the same step (no reader could see it pending).
# - The page's CatchUp is folded into every append the same way; what
#   the page shows of status is `status`, derived from disk as serve does.
# - PartialWrite is its own step, Tear: the fragment is the same whether
#   ENOSPC cut the line or a crash did, and the adapter can make one by
#   appending bytes with no newline; which failing write tears is not
#   something a test can choose.
# - ResumedContextDiffers is Prompt on a gone child with pending set: the
#   resumed child reads the disk, which lacks what was lost. Nothing
#   observable distinguishes it beyond pending/warn, so it has no field.
# - Read faults are one at a time (fault), and a new one waits until the
#   page has seen the session healthy again: combinations are the union
#   of their effects, and without the wait a fault re-injected before
#   every poll would starve "the session reappears" in a way no product
#   could fix.
# - Subscribe is part of OpenSession (the page opens the session and its
#   stream together).

# status the page should show: what the child did.
def truth(turn):
    return turn

# status serve derives from the file (StatusOf).
def derive(ondisk, child):
    if ondisk == "open":
        if child == "alive":
            return "running"
        return "interrupted"
    return "done"

role Session:
    action Init:
        # One finished turn is on disk; the child is alive and idle.
        self.disk = "ok"        # ok | full: whether writes can land
        self.child = "alive"    # alive | gone
        self.turn = "done"      # what the child did: running | done | interrupted
        self.ondisk = "closed"  # the file's last turn: open (input, no done) | closed
        self.tail = "clean"     # clean | torn: a fragment with no newline ends the file
        self.glued = False      # a line written after a fragment is glued to it (unreadable)
        self.pending = False    # the child holds entries the file lacks
        self.warn = False       # the page says history is not being saved
        self.fault = "none"     # none | corrupt | oversize | file | dir
        self.list = "listed"    # GET /api/sessions: listed | missing | empty | error
        self.open = "shown"     # GET /api/sessions/{id}: shown | partial | missing | toolong | error
        self.status = "done"    # the row's status, derived from disk

    # One write attempt by the live child: pending entries first, then
    # the new one (turn already updated by the caller).
    atomic func write():
        if self.disk == "full":
            # Today: the line is dropped (never pending) and the page is
            # only told to refetch (warn stays False).
            self.pending = True
            self.warn = True
        else:
            # Today: no truncation; the first line lands glued to the
            # fragment (self.glued = True) and is skipped on every read.
            self.tail = "clean"
            self.pending = False
            self.warn = False
            if self.turn == "running":
                self.ondisk = "open"
            else:
                self.ondisk = "closed"
        self.status = derive(self.ondisk, self.child)

    # --- system: the disk ---

    atomic action DiskFills:
        require self.disk == "ok"
        self.disk = "full"

    atomic fair action DiskFrees:
        require self.disk == "full"
        self.disk = "ok"

    # A write cut part way (ENOSPC mid-line, or a crash): a fragment
    # with no newline ends the file.
    atomic action Tear:
        require self.tail == "clean"
        self.tail = "torn"

    # --- the child ---

    # POST /api/sessions/{id}/prompt. A gone child is resumed first
    # (ensure, `-r <id>`): OpenExisting drops a torn tail, reads the file
    # (so what was pending is lost from its context), closes the dangling
    # turn as cancelled and the input opens a new one; both are writes.
    # With the file or the dir unreadable there is no session to send to.
    # Today: an oversize line fails OpenExisting and the resume.
    atomic action Prompt:
        require self.turn != "running" and self.fault in ("none", "corrupt", "oversize")
        if self.child == "gone":
            self.child = "alive"
            self.tail = "clean"
            self.pending = False
        self.turn = "running"
        self.write()

    # The turn ends (llm-control releases it) and the loop records done.
    atomic fair action Finish:
        require self.turn == "running"
        self.turn = "done"
        self.write()

    # The store's retry tick: pending entries are written once space is
    # back even when the child is idle. Strongly fair: DiskFills can
    # disable it again and again. Today: does not exist.
    atomic fair<strong> action Flush:
        require self.child == "alive" and self.pending and self.disk == "ok"
        self.write()

    # The child exits or crashes. What it held pending is gone with it.
    atomic action Exit:
        require self.child == "alive"
        self.child = "gone"
        if self.turn == "running":
            self.turn = "interrupted"
        self.status = derive(self.ondisk, self.child)

    # The turn writes one entry over 4 MiB (a huge tool result).
    atomic action WriteHugeEntry:
        require self.turn == "running" and self.disk == "ok" and self.fault == "none" and self.list == "listed" and self.open == "shown"
        self.fault = "oversize"

    # --- system: damage and repair ---

    atomic action CorruptLine:
        require self.fault == "none" and self.list == "listed" and self.open == "shown"
        self.fault = "corrupt"

    atomic action Chmod000:
        require self.fault == "none" and self.list == "listed" and self.open == "shown"
        self.fault = "file"

    atomic action ChmodDir:
        require self.fault == "none" and self.list == "listed" and self.open == "shown"
        self.fault = "dir"

    # chmod back, delete the bad line or the huge entry.
    atomic fair action Repair:
        require self.fault != "none"
        self.fault = "none"

    # --- the page ---

    # The list poll (4 s). Today: dir -> "empty"; file, oversize -> "missing".
    atomic fair action ListPoll:
        if self.fault == "dir":
            self.list = "error"
        else:
            self.list = "listed"

    # Opening the session (GET + subscribe), or its catch-up after an
    # event. Today: dir, file, oversize -> "missing" (404 unknown session).
    atomic fair action OpenSession:
        if self.fault in ("dir", "file"):
            self.open = "error"
        else:
            self.open = "shown"

action Init:
    session = Session()

# While appends fail the page shows history is not being saved.
always assertion PageWarnsWhileNotSaving:
    return not session.pending or session.warn

# A line written after a failed (torn) one is readable.
always assertion AppendAfterFailureReadable:
    return not session.glued

# The status read off disk is what the child did, or the page is saying
# why it cannot be (history not saved).
always assertion StatusAgreesOrWarned:
    return session.status == truth(session.turn) or session.warn

# The file always exists here: it is never "unknown" (404) nor left out
# of a 200 list.
always assertion SessionNeverUnknown:
    return session.open != "missing" and session.list != "missing"

# An unreadable dir is a 500 with a reason, never an empty 200.
always assertion ListNeverEmptyOnDirError:
    return session.list != "empty"

# Every entry size history writes can be read back.
always assertion EverySizeReadsBack:
    return session.open != "toolong"

# A corrupt line never hides the rest of its session.
always assertion CorruptLineHidesNothing:
    return session.open != "partial"

# After Repair the session reappears and opens, with no reload.
always eventually assertion SessionReappears:
    return session.list == "listed" and session.open == "shown"

# After DiskFrees what was lost reaches the file and the page: a live
# child's status comes to agree with what it did.
always eventually assertion StatusConverges:
    return session.child == "gone" or session.status == truth(session.turn)
